course: dictionary
lesson: 7931
title: Realise: suddenly understanding something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To realise means to suddenly understand something, or to become aware of it. «Jake realised he could not remember why he had hit the other boy.» Jake did not know this until he thought about it, and then he understood it. That is what realise means here.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Phrases like «did not realise» or «suddenly realise» show that something was not understood yet. «Many pets end up in rescue centres because their owners did not realise how much care they need.» So the owners did not understand this before.
explain: Realise can also mean to make a dream or plan come true. Check the sentence: if "understand" does not fit, the meaning is probably "make come true". Swapping your meaning into the sentence is always a good check.
fact: Realise means to suddenly understand or become aware of something.
fact: To realise a dream or plan means to make it come true.
fact: Realise is a verb, so it changes: realises, realised, realising.
fact: British spelling is realise; American spelling is realize.
fact: «Realised» can show a turning point in a story, such as «She realised she was lost».
exercise: «Jake realised he could not remember why he had hit the other boy.» What does realised mean here? | *Suddenly understood | Ran away | Forgot completely | Shouted loudly
exercise: Ella says, «I want to realise my dream of becoming a vet.» What does realise mean? | To forget about the dream | *To make the dream come true | To sleep through the dream | To tell everyone about the dream
exercise: Which word fits best? «She ___ she was lost in the woods.» | *realised | rescued | climbed | painted
test: «Sam did not realise his bag was open until the bus pulled away.» What does did not realise mean? | Wanted to keep it | *Did not notice or understand | Had lost it on purpose | Was happy about it
test: Which phrase means to make a plan come true? | *Realise the plan | Hide the plan | Read the plan | Forget the plan
exam: Which word could replace realised in «She realised she was lost»? | Sold | Painted | Closed | *Understood
